</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Often through my heart is pealing</l><l>Many another voice than Thine,</l><l>Many an unwilled echo stealing</l><l>From the walls of this Thy shrine.</l><l>Let Thy longed-for accents fall;</l><l>Master, speak! and silence all.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Master, speak! though least and lowest,</l><l>Let me not unheard depart;</l><l>Master, speak! for oh, Thou knowest</l><l>All the yearning of my heart.</l><l>Knowest all its truest need;</l><l>Speak! and make me blest indeed.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Master, speak! and make me ready,</l><l>When Thy voice is truly heard,</l><l>With obedience glad and steady,</l><l>Still to follow every word</l><l>I am listening, Lord, for Thee:</l><l>Master, speak, oh, speak to me!</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Speak to me by name, O Master,</l><l>Let me know it is to me;</l><l>Speak, that I may follow faster,</l><l>With a step more firm and free,</l><l>Where the Shepherd leads the flock</l><l>In the shadow of the Rock!</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
